; hawkesgen.com for Cloudflare (DNS > Records > Import and Export > Import). Rebuilt 2026-10-28 after Route 53 stopped
; answering: Firebase's own record list, the Hawkes Net VM, Resend's sending records. Every record is DNS only (grey
; cloud): Firebase and Caddy issue their own certificates and need to see the real address.
$ORIGIN hawkesgen.com.
$TTL 300
; The portal: Firebase Hosting, project hawkes-prod (hostState, ownership and certificate all ACTIVE).
@                    300 IN A     199.36.158.100
www                  300 IN A     199.36.158.100
@                    300 IN TXT   "hosting-site=hawkes-prod"
; Hawkes Net (Google VM hawkes-net, us-east4-c).
net                  300 IN A     34.86.89.28
; Email sent as support@ through Resend.
resend._domainkey    300 IN TXT   "p=MIGfMA0GCSqGSIb3DQEBAQUAA4GNADCBiQKBgQC3CsYE2fBa5I6hBit66WY30fh0urIevB447V/+rW6QxBVJxgHkbrdZbLY1lTa2L8r9VlRnmZW0UoGD6z8bIBXAtA7H1kBlQO/i+aPPrBaL0sHAmnfCQd6FyuWwMcnaKP79GTYtzm2HEIqL3NXR18+Uyt83wjOfqszDUwV9ZspNQwIDAQAB"
rsend                300 IN CNAME rsend.forge.rmta.net.
send                 300 IN CNAME send.forge.rmta.net.
_dmarc               300 IN TXT   "v=DMARC1; p=none;"
; Not here on purpose (see README.md): studio, gen, the beta sites and cdn were on the AWS control server and its S3,
; which no longer answer; hawkesnet (beta Net) and the old MX (SES inbound) were AWS too. Mail to support@ comes back
; through Cloudflare Email Routing, which adds its own MX and SPF records when it's turned on.
